    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "It is well-known that polymorphism is common in active pharmaceutical ingredients (APIs), which can lead to diverse physicochemical properties such as solubility, hygroscopicity, stability, dissolution, etc., further aff",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "1",
     "4"
    ],
    "n": 2
   },
   {
    "frase": "The disappearing ritonavir form event is a typical example, where a phase transformation occurred during the production process, resulting in serious economic losses [5].",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "5"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Therefore, a comprehensive characterization and phase transformation study of polymorph and determination of thermodynamic relationships between the different forms can assist in the selection of the best solid form for ",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "6",
     "8"
    ],
    "n": 2
   },
   {
    "frase": "In addition, it is important to understand the selective nucleation of different polymorphs so that polymorphism can be precisely regulated and predicted to guide product and process development [9,10].",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "9,10"
    ],
    "n": 1
